This repository sets up Road Trip Adventure (PlayStation 2; Road Trip in
North America, Choro Q HG 2 in Japan) on ARM64 Linux handhelds with ARMSX2,
the ARM64 PlayStation 2 emulator: https://github.com/ARMSX2/ARMSX2, GPL-3.0,
derived from PCSX2 (https://pcsx2.net). The scripts download ARMSX2's own
Linux arm64 AppImage from its releases on the device; none of it is stored
here, and nothing in this repository is derived from its code.

The Steam artwork is downloaded at install time from libretro-thumbnails:
https://github.com/libretro-thumbnails/Sony_-_PlayStation_2. It is not
stored here.

The launcher and the Steam scripts come from the FIFA Street ARM64 port
(https://github.com/Ken5998/fifa-street-arm64) by the same author.

No game files and no BIOS are included: the player uses their own disc image
and the BIOS dumped from their own PlayStation 2.
